{
  "id": "Compound::DB01019 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Bethanechol, a cholinergic agonist, is implicated in the interaction with Chrm2 and Chrm3 through a shared pathway involving G-protein coupled receptors. The evidence suggests that Bethanechol binds to Chrm2, which is a key component of G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity or muscarinic acetylcholine receptors, both of which are involved in the activation of Chrm3. This indicates a potential mechanism where Bethanechol modulates Chrm3 through the activation of Chrm2, which in turn activates G-protein pathways. The overlapping roles of Chrm2 in different receptor activities suggest a general involvement in the signaling cascade that leads to Chrm3 activation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Chrm2 as a central mediator in the interaction between Bethanechol and Chrm3, emphasizing the importance of G-protein coupled receptors in the downstream effects of cholinergic stimulation.",
